# SplitWorkspace thread-local cache — paired A/B wall-clock measurement
# Date: 2026-05-16
# Repo state (jj change): ynkmxszz (pre-commit working copy)
# Parent (main):          pwwusplv (1fbb4ba8 docs: lossless e7 1024² at 1.2× cjxl with parallel-tree-learning)
#
# Goal: eliminate per-fork SplitWorkspace::new ~12 MB allocations in the
# parallel-tree-learning path (rayon agent's 2026-05-16 memory note flagged
# this as the measured Amdahl ceiling on the parallel tree builder).
#
# Hardware: AMD Ryzen 9 7950X (16C/32T) water-cooled, 128 GB RAM
# OS:       WSL2 Linux 6.6
# Compiler: rustc 1.93 (release profile, NO -C target-cpu=native — runtime SIMD only)
# Build:    cargo build -p jxl-encoder-cli --release --features parallel-tree-learning --bin cjxl-rs
#
# Binaries:
#   cjxl-rs-baseline = main@origin (1fbb4ba8) + parallel-tree-learning feature
#   cjxl-rs-splitws  = baseline + thread-local SplitWorkspace cache
#                      (this change). Replaces per-call SplitWorkspace::new
#                      with `with_thread_local_workspace(...)` at all 5
#                      call sites (compute_best_tree_with_budget root +
#                      sequential loop, build_subtree_sequential,
#                      build_subtree_recursive_parallel,
#                      compute_best_tree_with_multipliers).
#
# Command per row:
#   RAYON_NUM_THREADS=8 <binary> <png> /tmp/_bench.jxl -e 7 --lossless
#
# Iterations: 10 per (image, binary), interleaved A/B (BASE → SPLITWS alternating)
# Warmup:     1 BASE + 1 SPLITWS per image before timing
#
# Hash-lock verification: all 3 images byte-identical between baseline and
# splitws at RAYON_NUM_THREADS={1, 4, 8, 16}:
#   small_0.26MP:   sha256 d16f994ab0026a2a (156321 bytes)
#   medium_1.05MP:  sha256 703a054799e77e7d (1281763 bytes)
#   large_4.19MP:   sha256 9bee1b66ce79bed4 (2762508 bytes)
# Plus all 36 cases in tests/hash_lock_features.rs pass byte-identical at
# default features AND with --features parallel-tree-learning.
#
# Allocation count (heaptrack, medium 1.05 MP):
#   baseline: 63630 total alloc calls, 232.89M peak heap
#   splitws:  63434 total alloc calls (-196), 232.89M peak heap (same)
# Allocation count (heaptrack, large 4.19 MP):
#   baseline: 90385 total alloc calls, 931.32M peak heap
#   splitws:  90185 total alloc calls (-200), 931.32M peak heap (same)
#   diff_log: -684 fewer top-frame allocator calls (most under
#             with_thread_local_workspace → 10 SplitWorkspace::new total,
#             one per rayon worker; remainder are 14 inner Vecs ×
#             ~16 forks that the old per-fork SplitWorkspace::new path made).
# Peak memory unchanged: TreeSamples (~150 MB) and PNG pixel buffers (~80 MB)
# dominate; SplitWorkspaces are 1–12 MB each, the cache pins one per worker.
#
# Profile images:
#   small_0.26MP   = /home/lilith/work/codec-corpus/CID22/CID22-512/training/7256805.png
#   medium_1.05MP  = /home/lilith/work/codec-corpus/clic2025-1024/02809272...png
#   large_4.19MP   = /home/lilith/work/codec-corpus/clic2025/final-test/8426ed22...png
#
# Background load: load average dropped from ~35 (extract_features_372col
# running) to ~3.5 during the run. Iters 1-2 had higher noise; iters 3-10
# under load < 5 are tight (max-min spread 50-80 ms at medium, 60-180 ms at large).
#
# Summary (10 iters per cell):
#   small_0.26MP:   305.5 → 308.1 mean (+0.85%, statistically tied)
#                   300.7 → 298.6 best-iter (-0.7%)
#   medium_1.05MP:  1891  → 1841  mean (-2.6%)
#                   1850  → 1810  best-iter (-2.2%)
#   large_4.19MP:   4698  → 4657  mean (-0.9%)
#                   4580  → 4570  best-iter (-0.2%)
#
# Mean improvement is largest on medium (1.05 MP) at -2.6%. Smaller-than-
# projected gain because:
#   1. `vec![0; N]` calloc on Linux with transparent hugepages is fast
#      (page-fault-on-write rather than upfront memset).
#   2. Each worker only allocates ONCE per encode regardless of fork count;
#      with 8 workers and 16 leaf tasks, the saved work is ~8 × calloc-time
#      not 16 × calloc-time. Calloc-time is the actual saved work, not the
#      full allocation-and-free pair.
#   3. The 1.67× internal speedup in compute_best_tree on 8 cores (rayon
#      agent's measurement) was bounded by something else — likely
#      `split_off` owned-clone overhead in `split_tree_samples_owned`
#      (also O(N log N) total) and work imbalance across leaf tasks.
#
# Allocation behavior is now structurally bounded: with the cache, total
# SplitWorkspace allocations across an entire encode = number of distinct
# rayon worker threads (verified by `test_thread_local_workspace_caps_allocations`
# Layer-2 invariant test). Before, each `find_best_split` call allocated a
# fresh ~12 MB workspace; the leak-count diff in heaptrack confirms only
# 10 SplitWorkspace allocations now live to end-of-program (one cached per
# worker), versus ~25 cumulative allocations in the baseline.
#
# Columns: image  threads  binary  iter  time_ms  bytes
